caveats:
1. Status: this is a brand-new arXiv v1 preprint (cs.AI) posted 2026-10-05, one day before this check. It is not peer-reviewed. The code link is an anonymous mirror (anonymous.4open.science/r/hear-3D1E), which suggests the paper is under double-blind review. The paper includes an AI-use statement covering methodology refinement, code, result interpretation and writing.
2. Possible conflict of interest: co-authors Jitai Hao and Jun Yu are authors of OmniKV (ref [10]). OmniKV is one of the evaluated execution modes, and it is in the selected DeepResearchBench mapping (OmniKV–H2O).
3. Hardware and scale are small and mixed. SCBench ran Qwen3-8B on a single RTX PRO 6000 (not an H100). Mooncake ran Qwen3-8B on a single H100. Both used a 96-GiB L2 KV cache. BrowseComp-Plus and DeepResearchBench ran GLM-4.7-Flash, with Main and Reader/sub-agent each on its own H100. Dense mode used vLLM 0.26.0;
